find /path/to/files* -mtime +5 -exec rm {} \;

 -mtime, is used to specify the number of days old that the file is.
-mtime n → files modified exactly n days ago
-mtime -n → files modified within last n days
-mtime +n → files modified more than n days ago

 -exec runs a command on each file found by find, where {} is the file(placeholder for the current file found) and \; ends the command.

Get list of files which are older than 5 days.

# find /root/ -mtime +5 -type f -exec ls -lrt {} \;

name pattern
# find /root/ -name '*cookie*' -mtime +5 -type f -exec ls -lrt {} \;

After checking and confirming the output go for file removal script.

# find /root/ -name '*cookie*' -mtime +5 -type f -exec rm -fv {} \;


